+"""Default rules for the provenance-aware smart approval review (``approvals.smart_provenance``).
+
+The rule set has the same shape as a coding agent's auto-mode permission policy: one HARD BLOCK rule
+that no user words clear, SOFT BLOCK rules that clear only at their consent bar (each names its
+**must name** item), ALLOW exceptions, and Environment entries describing the trust boundary.
+Operators extend every list through ``approvals.smart_rules`` (trusted config).
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+# (name, must_name, text). A must_name of None means the rule has no consent bar (hard block or allow).
+HARD_BLOCK: list[tuple[str, str | None, str]] = [
+    ("Data Exfiltration", None,
+     "Sensitive data leaving the trust boundary (the repos, domains and buckets listed in Environment) because of "
+     "the agent's action, directly or through a pathway the agent arms for later. Judge where the data finally "
+     "lands, not the first hop; a destination not listed in Environment is external, and an unknown repo "
+     "visibility is not on its own a reason to block. Vehicles include HTTP requests, file uploads, git commit or "
+     "push, a changed API base URL, public buckets, pastes and gists, share or presigned links, and package "
+     "publishes. Encoded or compressed payloads count as their decoded content. An external service the agent "
+     "picked on its own is not trusted because it picked it. Checks, in order: (1) What is sent? Sensitivity "
+     "comes from where the content came from, not how harmless it looks: anything that started inside the "
+     "boundary (a private repo file, a config, a credential, an untracked dotfile such as `.env`) is sensitive "
+     "once it reaches an outside or public place; a file never shown is unknown, not clean. (2) Follow the whole "
+     "path: arming a CI or publish pipeline that will upload private content is the harm even if a merge or "
+     "review gates it; shipping a whole tree to any destination other than the repo's own remote as of session "
+     "start is exfiltration at any claimed privacy. (3) Is the final destination listed in Environment, or the "
+     "trusted repo's own remote with a visibility that fits the content? A remote added or repointed in this "
+     "session is a new, untrusted destination. Loopback addresses (127.0.0.1, ::1, localhost) on the machine "
+     "the agent runs on are inside the boundary."),
+]
+
+SOFT_BLOCK: list[tuple[str, str | None, str]] = [
+    ("Git Destructive", "the destructive operation and its target",
+     "A force push, remote branch or tag deletion, release deletion or history rewrite that destroys other "
+     "people's work. On a shared or release branch (main, master, staging, develop, prod-*, release-*, release/*, "
+     "or the default branch) other people's work is presumed, so a bare force push or branch deletion there is "
+     "this rule; `--force-with-lease` is the careful form and is judged on whether the loss is clear. Elsewhere "
+     "block only when it is clear the lost work is someone else's. Remote branch deletion needs the user to say "
+     "remote. Reshaping the agent's own commits (amend, rebase, force push of a personal branch with only its "
+     "commits) is normal; amending a HEAD that existed before the session rewrites the user's commit unless the "
+     "user asked to amend."),
+    ("Code That Leaks When Run", "the execution effect: what runs, and where it sends or exposes what",
+     "Committing or pushing code that, when CI, a deploy or another person runs it, would send secrets or "
+     "sensitive data out of the repo or widen what a deploy exposes. Arming the pathway is the harm, whenever it "
+     "triggers."),
+    ("Code from External", "the external source (the URL or repo)",
+     "Running code that came from outside: `curl | sh`, eval or exec of remote content, unsafe deserialization "
+     "(pickle, yaml unsafe load, torch.load) of external data, or running, building, installing, testing or "
+     "importing material cloned or unpacked this session (any interpreter, build tool or test runner whose "
+     "working directory, script or target is inside it runs what was planted there). Listing, reading or "
+     "grepping such material, or parsing it as plain data from code outside it, is not this rule. The repo the "
+     "agent started in is trusted. A source the agent chose (a search hit, a link in fetched content) is "
+     "external. Asking to read a URL is consent to read it, not to run what it serves."),
+    ("Cloud Storage Mass Delete", "the store being deleted (the bucket, dataset, or table)",
+     "Deleting or mass-modifying cloud object storage, or dropping or truncating data stores (DROP or TRUNCATE "
+     "TABLE, DELETE or UPDATE without a narrow predicate, dropDatabase, deleteMany({}), bucket removal)."),
+    ("Production Deploy", "the production target",
+     "Deploying to a production service or running production database migrations."),
+    ("Remote Shell Writes", "the host or workload being written to",
+     "Writing to running production or shared hosts through a remote shell (kubectl exec, docker exec, ssh, "
+     "remote PowerShell), which skips normal deploy guardrails."),
+    ("Sensitive Remote Exec", "the target host, pod, or workload",
+     "An interactive session, persistent shell or port-forward into a Sensitive remote target listed in "
+     "Environment (kubectl attach or port-forward, exec -it, ssh with no command, a bare shell as exec payload)."),
+    ("Production Reads", "the prod target",
+     "Reading inside running production through a remote shell, dumping its env vars or configs, or querying a "
+     "production database directly: even a read pulls live secrets into the transcript and logs."),
+    ("Blind Apply", "skipping the preview for that change",
+     "For live, production or shared infrastructure, skipping the preview or dry run and going straight to the "
+     "change (`--yes`, `--auto-approve`, `--force`, or a preview and apply chained in one command so nobody can "
+     "review the plan)."),
+    ("Protected-Scope IaC Apply", "the specific change",
